From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:14:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Dolby Vision: settings, strings and player information

- Settings > Player > Dolby Vision (category dolbyvision): output mode
  (Dolby Vision (TV-led), Convert to HDR10, Convert to HDR10+ or Off,
  listed only where the connection has them: OutputModeOptions), HDR10+
  videos, enhancement layer upscaling (Annex B Master Reference or
  bilinear), Dolby Vision metadata (original, CM4.0 auto, CM4.0 always;
  TV peak brightness), Remove L2 trims, enhanced player information,
  the menu output (Dolby Vision for the menu, brightness, saturation,
  gamma, wide colour), reuse of unchanged controls and the home screen,
  half-resolution menus, and developer switches (verify output, frame
  and GPU timing logs). yblod.build lets skins detect YBLOD;
  dvbridge.settingsversion records settings migrations.
- DVOutputSettings.h latches the output preferences when playback is
  prepared (SelectOutputSettings), so an open settings dialog cannot
  change a running title; DVEngineSettings.h applies the engine's
  settings as environment overrides at start and on every change,
  taking precedence over native-dv.env.
- The fork's strings use ids 45000 to 45999, a block Kodi does not use,
  so that they cannot collide with strings Kodi adds. #40818 ("Player
  information") is kept beside #45018: the pre-installed
  skin.estuary.yblod add-on shows $LOCALIZE[40818] and updates on its
  own schedule.
- Player information (O): Estuary's panel (IncludesDVProcessInfo.xml)
  shows video, audio, Dolby Vision metadata and the GPU's render usage;
  turning enhanced player information off restores Kodi's panel.
  RenderUsage (DVRenderUsage.cpp) reads the i915/xe engine time of
  Kodi's own DRM descriptors from fdinfo, opening only descriptors known
  to be DRM files. VideoGUIInfo reports HDMI Dolby Vision only for
  output that was presented (CDVPlaybackInfo), not for the source's
  format.
- Telemetry: DVStreamTelemetry follows the stream, its decoded format
  and the drop and skip counters for the panel. VideoPlayerVideo writes
  a "DVBridge playback health" line every 10 s of native playback only
  with DVBRIDGE_DIAGNOSTICS=1 (at INFO) or debug logging (at DEBUG), and
  samples nothing otherwise.

Settings.cpp registers the options filler and the HDR10+ condition
under HAVE_DVBRIDGE. The renderer, window and engine adapter
(kodi-9956, kodi-9957) read these settings; the panel shows what the
decoder (kodi-9952) and the window report.

Formerly kodi-9996-output-modes-and-info (most of it) and the playback
information of kodi-9990-native-dv, with yblod-02 (menu output), -18
(Dolby Vision category), -21 (engine settings), -23, -31, -32 (Dolby
Vision menu), -34 (HDR10+), -54 (string ids), -57 (diagnostics cost)
and -59 (the render code's strings by their new ids).
